# Milestone: M3
# Covers: at() watcher persists across multiple condition checks; chunk does not
#         quiesce until the condition becomes true.
#
# defer-to: M5
#
# Reason: at() bare watcher syntax and persistent-watcher semantics land at M5
# (reactive-runtime). At M3, OP_AT is emitted as a stub that returns
# URBI_ERR_NOTIMP.
#
# When M5 lands, implement this fixture by uncommenting the urbiscript source
# below. Expected behaviour: the chunk sets x = 0, then registers an at(x == 1)
# watcher that prints a message. The chunk does not quiesce until x becomes 1.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at M5):
#   var x = 0;
#   at (x == 1) { echo("x is one") };
#   x = 1;
#   --- expected output (with deterministic watcher firing) ---
#   [00000001] 1
#   [00000002] "x is one"
